essure to your piping bag and  move in a very subtle  circular motion and then top it off with  some flowers  no rhyme or reason here just do what  makes you happy  [Applause]  topping off your cake with flowers is  usually a safe bet  and those flowers look so good  let's take a break from crumb coats and  talk flower piping techniques  to make some beautiful buttercream roses  you're going to need this petal piping  tip  add that to your piping bag and then  fill it with red buttercream frosting  now this is called a flower nail it's  just a very handy tool that's going to  make it really easy to sculpt our roses  first place a dab of buttercream on the  nail and place a square of parchment  paper on top  touch the wide end of the tip to the  base of the flower nail and the narrow  end  should point up an angle slightly inward  squeeze  the bag and rotate the nail use even  pressure to squeeze out the next petal  touch the tip to the base of the center  bud and rotate the nail  as you squeeze creating ribbons that  wrap halfway around  make sure each new petal overlaps the  one before it  and there you have it buttercream roses  but you know what we're feeling festive  so  let's do some poinsettias next the only  thing you'll need different is this leaf  piping tip create leaves by squeezing  hard at the base and then release the  pressure  as you pull out poinsettias have five  leaves at the bottom  and another five stacked on top to  really sell it  we're going to add gold sprinkles right  in the center of our leaves  perfect now we're just going to put all  of our flowers on a baking sheet  and transfer them to the fridge to chill  to complete this technique we use this  basket weave piping tip and filled our  piping bag with white buttercream  but hey dealer's choice you'll need a  second coat of buttercream  on your cake before you start decorating  and when you're ready  take your piping bag and use even  pressure to pipe out  one long strip straight down now do a  shorter horizontal strip  over that keep making this horizontal  strips all the way down  leaving an empty space about the size of  the piping tip  in between each strip now make your next  vertical strip  down covering one edge of those  horizontal strips  start your next set of horizontal  stripes by burying the piping tip  under the previous vertical line now  it's just repeating the pattern from  here  keep creating your lines and stripes  until you've completely covered your  cake  now you could stop right here if you've  never decorated a cake before  this is way beyond impressive but take  it up a notch and bring back those  poinsettias and roses that we made  earlier and decorate the top of your  cake with flowers  now that looks great for these empty  spaces  we're going to bring back our leaf  piping tip filled with  green buttercream we're going to create  some leaves in there  using the same technique we use to  create our poinsettias just squeeze  hard at the base and release pressure as  you pull out  now that is an awesome cake it feels  very festive because of the colors that  we used but you can recreate this  technique for  any occasion in any color that you like  and it's going to look  great guaranteed now let's finish up  with an easy approach to a geode cake  add a second layer of buttercream on top  of your crumb coat ours is blue and we  save some of that blue frosting to use  to decorate with later this is our rock  candy that we're going to use for our  geode pattern and this is blue food  coloring and vodka  which we'll use to dye our candy using a  small serrated knife  carve out a space in the cake where your  rock candy will sit  you can make this whichever size you  prefer just clean out the space so it's  a bit more even but it doesn't have to  be perfect because we're going to use  that extra buttercream we saved to cover  this back up  once that's recoated it's time to add  our rock candy just cover up  any space that you see and press down  firm to make sure the rock candy sits in  your frosting wall  now for that vodka and food coloring  mixture take a little bit  and paint it on the innermost wall of  the rock candy this is going to give  your cake  more depth you'll need to chill this for  about 20 minutes before doing  anything else to jazz it up a little  we're going to add  gold leaf around the edges  all of these cakes can be easily  customized to match your style  and the techniques will get easier and  easier the more you try them  for more cake decorating techniques  check out our  other tasty video five beautiful ways to  decorate a cake  for more delicious baking content follow  fluff cups on instagram  if you try any of these techniques at  home make sure you tag  us on all your recreations  oh yes  you
 

